-- SWITCH STATEMENT --------------------------------------------- main.kl  K0925

`switch`, `case X ->` and `x => …` arms come from other languages. Kalam branches on a value with `match` and one `case pattern:` line per arm.

2│     switch n {
       ^^^^^^^^^^

Try:

    match n:
        case 0: return "zero"

Help: Write `match x:` and, indented under it, `case pattern: result` for each arm. Use `_` as the pattern for "anything else". `kalam fix` does this for you.

Learn more: kalam explain K0925
